Hi,

Just for your information with regard to grub2 packages in a few distro.

Recently, I found that debian sid update its grub2 package
and now the package includes nilfs2 module.

Also, ubuntu repository already has new version of grub2 with nilfs2.
http://mirrors.kernel.org/ubuntu/pool/main/g/grub2/grub-pc_1.98+20100614-2ubuntu4_i386.deb

You may not able to upgrade the package with aptitude but have to get
the package and install by dpkg.  I haven't tried but boot loader is
one of the most independent package, it may not be that hard to install.

So now you can boot kernel in nilfs2 filesystem without compiling
bootloader anymore.

enjoy!

Unfortunately, Fedora13 is still using grub-legacy, and
looks like there is no grub2 package. unnh.
http://fedoraproject.org/wiki/Features/Grub2
http://ftp.riken.jp/Linux/fedora/releases/13/Fedora/i386/os/Packages/


